---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import {kontainerSidebar} from '../../../data/kontainer-sidebar';
import {Code} from 'astro:components';
---

<DocsLayout title="Debugging / Introspection" sidebar={kontainerSidebar}
            description="Inspect the full service graph, track overrides, and debug your Kontainer at runtime">

    <h1>Debugging / Introspection</h1>

    <p class="text-xl text-gray-400 !mt-2 !mb-8">
        Every Kontainer is fully introspectable. Query the complete service graph at runtime &mdash;
        what is registered, how it's wired, what overrides what, and how often each service was created.
    </p>

    <h2>Dumping the container</h2>

    <p>For a quick overview, <code>dumpKontainer()</code> returns a human-readable table of all services, the
        built-ins included: each one's type, its kind, and what its provider created (count, first and last time):</p>

    <Code code={`val blueprint = kontainer {
    dynamic(RequestContext::class)
    singleton(Config::class)
    singleton(UserService::class)  // injects RequestContext
}

val kontainer = blueprint.create {
    with(RequestContext::class) { RequestContext("user-42") }
}
kontainer.get(UserService::class)

println(kontainer.tools.dumpKontainer())
// Kontainer dump:
//
// Service ID                                        | Type      | Kind                         | Created
// app.Config                                        | Singleton | Static                       |
// io.peekandpoke.ultra.kontainer.KontainerBlueprint | Singleton | Static                       |
// app.UserService                                   | Singleton | SemiDynamic (RequestContext) | 1, first 2026-11-25T10:30:00.004Z, last 2026-11-25T10:30:00.004Z
// app.RequestContext                                | Singleton | Dynamic (overridden)         | 1, first 2026-11-25T10:30:00.001Z, last 2026-11-25T10:30:00.001Z
// io.peekandpoke.ultra.kontainer.Kontainer          | Singleton | Dynamic                      |
// io.peekandpoke.ultra.kontainer.InjectionContext   | Singleton | Dynamic                      |`} lang="kotlin" theme="vitesse-dark"/>

    <p>A semi-dynamic service names the dynamic services that made it so. A global singleton is created in an internal
        kontainer shared by the whole blueprint, so it shows as created in every kontainer, while the prototypes it
        creates (directly or through <code>Lazy</code>, <code>List</code> or <code>Lookup</code>) show in no request's
        dump.</p>

    <h2>Types and kinds</h2>

    <p>Each service answers two questions. Its <strong>type</strong> (<code>ServiceType</code>) says what it is:
        <code>Singleton</code>, one shared instance, or <code>Prototype</code>, a new instance per injection. Its
        <strong>kind</strong> (<code>ServiceKind</code>) says what it is bound to:</p>

    <div class="not-prose my-8">
        <table class="w-full text-sm text-left">
            <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-white/10">
                <th class="py-2 text-white font-semibold">Kind</th>
                <th class="py-2 text-white font-semibold">Meaning</th>
            </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="text-gray-400">
            <tr class="border-b border-white/5">
                <td class="py-2"><code>Static</code></td>
                <td class="py-2">The same for every container of the blueprint; a static singleton is shared by all of them</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-white/5">
                <td class="py-2"><code>Dynamic</code></td>
                <td class="py-2">Declared as bound to one container: <code>dynamic</code> or <code>dynamicPrototype</code></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td class="py-2"><code>SemiDynamic</code></td>
                <td class="py-2">Declared static, but reaches a dynamic service through its injections, so bound to one container too</td>
            </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>

    <p>Only <code>Static</code> and <code>Dynamic</code> are declared; <code>SemiDynamic</code> is derived by the
        blueprint. <code>singleton</code> and <code>instance</code> declare (<code>Singleton</code>, <code>Static</code>),
        <code>dynamic</code> (<code>Singleton</code>, <code>Dynamic</code>), <code>prototype</code>
        (<code>Prototype</code>, <code>Static</code>) and <code>dynamicPrototype</code> (<code>Prototype</code>,
        <code>Dynamic</code>). For a prototype the kind changes nothing about when instances are created; it says
        whether the singletons injecting it become one per container. A dynamic singleton replaced at
        <code>create</code> is additionally flagged <code>overridden</code>.</p>

    <h2>Structured debug info</h2>

    <p>For programmatic access, <code>getDebugInfo()</code> returns the full service graph as structured data. Each
        service entry includes its type and kind, what it creates, what it injects, how often it was created, and
        whether it overrides another definition:
    </p>

    <Code code={`import io.peekandpoke.ultra.kontainer.domain.DebugInfo

val debugInfo = kontainer.tools.getDebugInfo()

debugInfo.services.forEach { service ->
    println("${'$'}{service.cls.fqn} [${'$'}{service.type}, ${'$'}{service.kind}, overridden=${'$'}{service.overridden}]")
    println("  created: ${'$'}{service.created.count}")

    // Why is it semi-dynamic? Empty for any other kind
    service.semiDynamicBecauseOf.forEach { println("  bound by: ${'$'}{it.fqn}") }

    // What does this service inject?
    service.definition.injects.forEach { param ->
        val lazy = if (param.provisionType == DebugInfo.ParamInfo.ProvisionType.Lazy) " (lazy)" else ""
        println("  -> ${'$'}{param.name}: ${'$'}{param.classes.map { it.fqn }}${'$'}{lazy}")
    }

    // Does this service override another definition?
    service.definition.overwrites?.let { overridden ->
        println("  overrides: ${'$'}{overridden.creates.fqn}")
    }
}`} lang="kotlin" theme="vitesse-dark"/>

    <p><code>definition.codeLocation.location</code> points to where a service was defined. For an override handed in
        at <code>create</code> it names the class in which the override lambda was written.</p>

    <h2>Querying the provider factory</h2>

    <p>For lower-level access, the <code>tools.factory</code> exposes the raw service providers:</p>

    <Code code={`val factory = kontainer.tools.factory

// All registered service providers
factory.getAllProviders().forEach { (cls, provider) ->
    println("${'$'}{cls.simpleName}: ${'$'}{provider.type}, ${'$'}{provider.kind}")
    println("  created: ${'$'}{provider.created.count}, first ${'$'}{provider.created.firstAt}")
    println("  dependencies: ${'$'}{provider.definition.producer.params.map { it.name }}")
}

// Has MyService been created in this kontainer? A singleton counts 0 or 1
val isCreated = kontainer.getProvider(MyService::class).created.count > 0`} lang="kotlin" theme="vitesse-dark"/>

    <h2>Tracking overrides</h2>

    <p>When a service is defined again within one blueprint (by a module and then the app, say) or replaced at
        <code>create</code>, the override chain is preserved. Walk the <code>overwrites</code> chain to see the full
        history. A definition from <code>extend</code> does not link to the one it replaced in the base blueprint.</p>

    <Code code={`val debugInfo = kontainer.tools.getDebugInfo()

debugInfo.services.forEach { service ->
    var def = service.definition
    var depth = 0

    while (def.overwrites != null) {
        depth++
        def = def.overwrites!!
        println("${'$'}{service.cls.fqn} override #${'$'}{depth}: was ${'$'}{def.creates.fqn}")
    }
}`} lang="kotlin" theme="vitesse-dark"/>

    <h2>Error handling</h2>

    <p>Kontainer throws specific exceptions for different problems:</p>

    <div class="not-prose my-8">
        <table class="w-full text-sm text-left">
            <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-white/10">
                <th class="py-2 text-white font-semibold">Exception</th>
                <th class="py-2 text-white font-semibold">When</th>
            </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="text-gray-400">
            <tr class="border-b border-white/5">
                <td class="py-2"><code>KontainerInconsistent</code></td>
                <td class="py-2">Dependency graph has problems (missing or ambiguous deps, cycles), or a registration or override is refused</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-white/5">
                <td class="py-2"><code>ServiceNotFound</code></td>
                <td class="py-2">Requested service is not registered</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-white/5">
                <td class="py-2"><code>ServiceAmbiguous</code></td>
                <td class="py-2">Multiple services match the requested type</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-white/5">
                <td class="py-2"><code>InvalidClassProvided</code></td>
                <td class="py-2">Tried to register an interface or abstract class directly</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td class="py-2"><code>InvalidServiceFactory</code></td>
                <td class="py-2">Factory method is invalid</td>
            </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>

    <div class="not-prose mt-8 flex gap-4">
        <a href="/ultra/kontainer/advanced"
           class="inline-flex items-center px-6 py-3 bg-white/5 text-gray-300 font-semibold rounded-lg hover:bg-white/10 transition-colors">
            &larr; Advanced Topics
        </a>
    </div>

</DocsLayout>
